7604706, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r577604706-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Holy tempel and big tempel aerea", "text": "The Tempel area is very big and nice to visit. It is similar like Varanasi. \nThe Sadhus the River the burning ghat the holy Tempel \nI would recommend it to everyone to visit when you are in Kathmandu.\nIt s a holy place for Hindus ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-05-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "3970E8062A2AAECE290B70FCCF14398B", "name": "Sussi S", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/9sussis", "username": "9sussis", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/ee/10/default-avatar-2020-8.jpg", "contribution_count": 171, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-05-03", "published_at_date": "2018-05-03"}, {"review_id": 577565375, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r577565375-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A very ancient temple and a good place to see!", "text": "Must see and visit. Take a guided tour so you get to know about the temple\nPS: Only Hindus are allowed in this temple, not even foreigners can enter the temple", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2018-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "15C0297982D6779E4AA28C46C0672640", "name": "Yogesh B", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/ybendre", "username": "ybendre", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/15/4d/df/47/ybendre.jpg", "contribution_count": 41, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304551, "location_name": "New Delhi", "location_name_detailed": "New Delhi, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-05-03", "published_at_date": "2018-05-03"}, {"review_id": 577515574, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r577515574-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Very Different Experience (Some Aspects Not So Pleasant)", "text": "This is a Hindu temple and the entry fee is NPR 1,600 per person; if you are a non-Hindu you can not access the temple complex.\n\nThe most elaborating aspect of this complex is the Hindu cremation process; at any given time you will find few dean bodies been set on fire and a few being prepared for cremation by families; the ash is washed away to the river which ties closely with the Hindu beliefs - a very sacred religious venue.\n\nYou have hermits but to take a photo comes at a cost - everything about this place is highly commercialised and found this to be not an uncomfortable experience (personal perspective).", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2018-05-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "16342FCB0BD139C21F3F5BE5C161243D", "name": "ClicknNomad", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/ClicknNomad", "username": "ClicknNomad", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0c/ec/e4/ff/avatar.jpg", "contribution_count": 126, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255103, "location_name": "Perth", "location_name_detailed": "Perth, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/12/d4/c1/55/photo0jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/12/d4/c1/56/photo1jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/12/d4/c1/57/photo2jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/12/d4/c1/58/photo3jpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2018-05-03", "published_at_date": "2018-05-03"}, {"review_id": 577320070, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r577320070-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "So Divine", "text": "A very nice temple, you have visit the temple from 930 A<M to 1130 Am.  during that time all the four doors are open and you can view five faces of pasupatinath.  You need to walk around to see the whole temple.  Felt very holy also scary because in that temple backside all death rituals are happening.  You can see the people waiting with their relative's dead body to perform last rites.  ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2018-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "2B93C0A8EFFAF3F12EE6D3C8AA4E665C", "name": "Gita R", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/saradhagita", "username": "saradhagita", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/77/ae/default-avatar-2020-2.jpg", "contribution_count": 9, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304551, "location_name": "New Delhi", "location_name_detailed": "New Delhi, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-05-02", "published_at_date": "2018-05-02"}, {"review_id": 577198216, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r577198216-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Worth a Visit", "text": "This is the USP of Nepal in addition to (of course) The Everest, lots of people visit this place both locals as well as Hindus from India. The gate of the temple opens up only at specific time. They perform Aarti just outside the temple everyday in the evening around 7pm which is worth watching.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "67B28334FB3C1D37B167EEB985BE2BCF", "name": "Tarang", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/jaintarang11", "username": "jaintarang11", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f6/0d/default-avatar-2020-34.jpg", "contribution_count": 236, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 494941, "location_name": "Indore", "location_name_detailed": "Indore, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-05-01", "published_at_date": "2018-05-01"}, {"review_id": 577102143, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r577102143-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "definitely not for the \"softer\" ones", "text": "If you want to enter the place, you have to pay 1000rupees. Before that, you get to see a local bazaar with paints and other traditional hindu things and some buildings which towards the sunset can give you the chills (great for photography).\nYou'll see there traditional funerals - cremations. It was my understanding that, to the left, they burnt the poorer ones, whereas to the right - the richer ones. The smell was a bit awful and eerie.\nIf you cross the bridge, you'll see a road leading you to a huge and beautiful park where you can find monkeys (BE mindful - they can rob you ;) ), cows among temples and deer kept behind a fence.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2018-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "5527E8A3824372294345FF8B41EE132A", "name": "Justyna H", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/945justynah", "username": "945justynah", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e2/e6/default-avatar-2020-45.jpg", "contribution_count": 15, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-05-01", "published_at_date": "2018-05-01"}, {"review_id": 577090841, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r577090841-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Not allowed inside", "text": "Should this really be on a UNESCO list if people from all backgrounds (i.e. non-Hindu) are not allowed to respectfully appreciate it?", "review_tip": null, "rating": 2, "subratings": [], "like_count": 3, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-05-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "C2C4AE34DC185B989A38CB9C48D8AD4E", "name": "rofo97", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/rofo97", "username": "rofo97", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/06/18/a5/eb/rofo97.jpg", "contribution_count": 1, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255068, "location_name": "Brisbane", "location_name_detailed": "Brisbane, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-05-01", "published_at_date": "2018-05-01"}, {"review_id": 577060342, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r577060342-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Interesting ", "text": "Hindu temple. Really enjoyed guided tour to learn more about the place and Hindu religion. Also you can see open cremation here. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [